---
.title = "Usage statistics",
.description = "Session metadata and usage counters serialized by LLMD for PostHog capture events.",
.date = .date("2026-11-27T00:00:00"),
.layout = "content.shtml",
.custom = .{ .doc_section = "Learn" },
---

LLMD send anonymous usage statistics to PostHog.
We use the following PostHog settings: `$process_person_profile = false` and `$geoip_disable = false`,
disabling user level statistics, but allowing coarse geographical localization.

We send statistics at startup time with LLMD version, selected backend, model type and cli flags.
We also collect some usage metric while serving.

The metrics are listed below.
They contain no user prompt, no generated text, embedding vectors, no model repository path or request body. 

Usage statistics can be disabled using [DO_NOT_TRACK]($link.page('llmd/reference/environment-variables').id('env-DO_NOT_TRACK') env variable.

# [User configuration]($heading.id('session-start'))

On session start we send the following properties,
describing how LLMD is used.

| Property | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| `timestamp_unix_ms` | Event timestamp in Unix milliseconds. |
| `llmd_revision` | LLMD revision for the session. |
| `model_type` | Model type for the session. |
| `api_kind` | Kind of API served. |
| `platform_target` | Platform target for the session. |
| `device_count` | Number of devices. |
| `device_kind` | Kind of device. |
| `configured_backend` | Configured execution backend. |
| `batch_size` | Configured batch size. |
| `token_batch_size` | Configured token batch size. |
| `max_context_length` | Configured maximum context length. |
| `prefill_chunk_size` | Configured prefill chunk size. |
| `page_chunk_size` | Configured KV-cache page chunk size. |
| `speculative_decoding_enabled` | Whether speculative decoding is enabled. |


# [Usage statistics]($heading.id('heartbeat-counters'))

During usage we send the following metrics,
to understand the relative importance of each configurations.

| Property | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| `input_tokens_total` | Total input tokens. |
| `prefill_tokens_total` | Total prefill tokens. |
| `output_tokens_total` | Total output tokens. |
| `requests_finished_eos_total` | Requests finished with an end-of-sequence condition. |
| `requests_finished_length_total` | Requests finished at a length limit. |
| `requests_finished_error_total` | Requests finished with an error. |
| `requests_finished_canceled_total` | Requests finished by cancellation. |
| `requests_rejected_oom_total` | Requests rejected due to an out-of-memory condition. |
| `embedding_inputs_completed_total` | Embedding inputs completed. |
| `embedding_inputs_error_total` | Embedding inputs with an error. |
| `embedding_inputs_canceled_total` | Embedding inputs canceled. |
| `embedding_inputs_rejected_oom_total` | Embedding inputs rejected due to an out-of-memory condition. |
